{
    "_comment": [
        "Physical locations of US National Weather Service Weather Forecast",
        "Offices (WFOs), keyed by the 3-letter site ID. Coordinates are ",
        "[lon, lat] in decimal degrees. Used by app.html to resolve each",
        "office's local timezone via @photostructure/tz-lookup so bulletin",
        "headers render in the WFO-local TZ (matching real NWS convention)",
        "even when the warned polygon lies in a different timezone.",
        "",
        "For example: KLBF (North Platte NE) is geographically in Central",
        "time, but its CWA extends west into the Nebraska Panhandle (Mountain",
        "time). A tornado warning for a polygon entirely in western Arthur/",
        "Grant/Hooker/McPherson counties still gets a bulletin dated",
        "'918 PM CDT Tue Jun 25 2024' -- primary = CDT (office local),",
        "secondary = MDT (polygon TZ) -- because the office is in Central.",
        "",
        "Coordinates are approximate (to the nearest 0.001 degree), sourced",
        "from NWS public office metadata, airport co-locations, and the",
        "publicly-documented physical addresses of each office. tz-lookup's",
        "IANA polygon resolution tolerates this level of precision well.",
        "Coordinates within ~5km of the real office location are fine;",
        "tz-lookup's nearest-polygon resolution doesn't care about that.",
        "",
        "The PQE / PQW entries are marine forecast areas without a physical",
        "office -- omitted here since they don't warn on storm polygons."
    ],
